# size: 1200x820
# diagnostic: GUI-02. The detail editors switch only on the task's column, so
# two tasks in one column share the native input lifetimes. Once two tasks in
# one column hold equal notes, selecting the second one retains the first
# task's editor — and with it the first task's undo history, which an ordinary
# Ctrl+Z then pastes into the wrong task. Native history depth is the
# observation neither the semantic specs nor a first-frame screenshot can make.
click #edit-task-2
wait 400
focus "Task notes"
key ctrl-a
key backspace
wait 600
expect-value "Task notes"
click #edit-task-1
wait 400
focus "Task notes"
key ctrl-a
key backspace
wait 600
type "Task notes" private
wait 600
key ctrl-a
key backspace
wait 600
expect-value "Task notes"
click #edit-task-2
wait 600
expect-value "Task notes"
expect-history "Task notes" 0
